teaches: DIFF
  draft    : Names the middle link of a soname chain (libfoo.so -> libfoo.so.1 -> libfoo.so.1.12) as the library's SONAME and warns that failing to follow that pattern may cause compatibility issues after an upgrade; the page never names DT_SONAME, so this row does not tie that tag to the link name.
  registry : The SONAME is a symlink in the middle of a chain that ldconfig creates; which file it names is install state that a regular-file digest cannot see.
